  _globals['_LOGSTREAMSERVICE'].methods_by_name['ListLogStreams']._serialized_options = b'\222A\272\005\n\013Log Streams\022\020List log streams\032\267\003Returns every log-streaming destination configured for the environment. Use this to render the log streaming settings page. The response also carries proxy_service_account_email, the service account a Google SecOps destination must be granted Chronicle log-ingest permission for. Each entry includes a masked credential hint, the derived delivery status, and the time of the most recent successful delivery; credentials are never returned.J\244\001\n\003200\022\234\001\nfLog streams listed successfully; includes the proxy service account email for Google SecOps IAM grants\0222\n0\032..scalekit.v1.logstreams.ListLogStreamsResponseJ8\n\003403\0221\n/Log streaming is not enabled for this workspace\202\265\030\002\030D\372\322\344\223\002\t\022\007PREVIEW\202\323\344\223\002\024\022\022/api/v1/logstreams'
  _globals['_LOGSTREAMSERVICE'].methods_by_name['GetLogStream']._loaded_options = None
  _globals['_LOGSTREAMSERVICE'].methods_by_name['GetLogStream']._serialized_options = b'\222A\354\003\n\013Log Streams\022\020Get a log stream\032\335\001Returns a single log-streaming destination by id. Use this to read one destination\'s current routing configuration, event filter, and derived delivery status. The credential is never returned \342\200\224 only a masked hint of it.J[\n\003200\022T\n Log stream returned successfully\0220\n.\032,.scalekit.v1.logstreams.GetLogStreamResponseJ8\n\003403\0221\n/Log streaming is not enabled for this workspaceJT\n\003404\022M\nKLog stream not found - no log stream with this id exists in the environment\202\265\030\002\030D\372\322\344\223\002\t\022\007PREVIEW\202\323\344\223\002\031\022\027/api/v1/logstreams/{id}'
  _globals['_LOGSTREAMSERVICE'].methods_by_name['CreateLogStream']._loaded_options = None
  _globals['_LOGSTREAMSERVICE'].methods_by_name['CreateLogStream']._serialized_options = b'\222A\311\010\n\013Log Streams\022\023Create a log stream\032\310\004Configures a new log-streaming destination for the environment. Use this when a customer adds a SIEM integration. Unless multiple destinations per provider are enabled for the environment, at most one destination per provider may exist and a duplicate create is rejected with a conflict. Datadog and CrowdStrike require credentials, which are validated against the destination before anything is saved; Google SecOps takes no credential and is authorized by an IAM grant on the proxy service account instead. The response returns the created destination with a masked credential hint.J]\n\003200\022V\n\037Log stream created successfully\0223\n1\032/.scalekit.v1.logstreams.CreateLogStreamResponseJ\240\001\n\003400\022\230\001\n\225\001Invalid request - provider or display name missing, credentials missing for Datadog or CrowdStrike, or the credential was rejected by the destinationJ8\n\003403\0221\n/Log streaming is not enabled for this workspaceJ\235\001\n\003409\022\225\001\n\222\001A log stream already exists for this provider in this environment (returned only while the environment is limited to one destination per provider)\202\265\030\002\030D\372\322\344\223\002\t\022\007PREVIEW\202\323\344\223\002 \"\022/api/v1/logstreams:\nlog_stream'
  _globals['_LOGSTREAMSERVICE'].methods_by_name['UpdateLogStream']._loaded_options = None
  _globals['_LOGSTREAMSERVICE'].methods_by_name['UpdateLogStream']._serialized_options = b'\222A\226\007\n\013Log Streams\022\023Update a log stream\032\374\003Changes a log-streaming destination\'s display name, routing configuration, event filter, or enabled state. Use this for edits and for pausing or resuming delivery. The provider is immutable: send it unchanged or omit it. Omitting credentials keeps the existing credential in place and leaves the masked hint untouched; supplying new credentials revalidates them against the destination before saving. The event filter is always applied exactly as sent, so an empty list restores delivery of every event type.J]\n\003200\022V\n\037Log stream updated successfully\0223\n1\032/.scalekit.v1.logstreams.UpdateLogStreamResponseJ\203\001\n\003400\022|\nzInvalid request - the provider does not match the existing log stream, or new credentials were rejected by the destinationJ8\n\003403\0221\n/Log streaming is not enabled for this workspaceJT\n\003404\022M\nKLog stream not found - no log stream with this id exists in the environment\202\265\030\002\030D\372\322\344\223\002\t\022\007PREVIEW\202\323\344\223\002%2\027/api/v1/logstreams/{id}:\nlog_stream'
  _globals['_LOGSTREAMSERVICE'].methods_by_name['DeleteLogStream']._loaded_options = None
  _globals['_LOGSTREAMSERVICE'].methods_by_name['DeleteLogStream']._serialized_options = b'\222A\213\004\n\013Log Streams\022\023Delete a log stream\032\254\002Removes a log-streaming destination and stops all delivery to it. Use this when a customer disconnects a SIEM integration. Delivery is torn down before the record is removed, so no destination keeps receiving events after this call returns. The stored credential is destroyed and cannot be recovered.J(\n\003200\022!\n\037Log stream deleted successfullyJ8\n\003403\0221\n/Log streaming is not enabled for this workspaceJT\n\003404\022M\nKLog stream not found - no log stream with this id exists in the environment\202\265\030\002\030D\372\322\344\223\002\t\022\007PREVIEW\202\323\344\223\002\031*\027/api/v1/logstreams/{id}'
  _globals['_LOGSTREAMSERVICE'].methods_by_name['TestLogStreamConnection']._loaded_options = None
  _globals['_LOGSTREAMSERVICE'].methods_by_name['TestLogStreamConnection']._serialized_options = b'\222A\361\005\n\013Log Streams\022\034Test a log stream connection\032\233\003Performs a real delivery to the configured destination and reports the outcome. Use this after configuring a destination to confirm the credential and routing actually work end to end. A rejected credential or unreachable destination is reported in the response body rather than as an error, so inspect success and message. Testing a disabled log stream returns success false without contacting the destination.J\225\001\n\003200\022\215\001\nNTest completed; inspect success and message for the destination\'s own response\022;\n9\0327.scalekit.v1.logstreams.TestLogStreamConnectionResponseJ8\n\003403\0221\n/Log streaming is not enabled for this workspaceJT\n\003404\022M\nKLog stream not found - no log stream with this id exists in the environment\202\265\030\002\030D\372\322\344\223\002\t\022\007PREVIEW\202\323\344\223\002+\"&/api/v1/logstreams/{id}:testConnection:\001*'
  _globals['_LOGSTREAMSERVICE'].methods_by_name['ListLogStreamDeliveries']._loaded_options = None
  _globals['_LOGSTREAMSERVICE'].methods_by_name['ListLogStreamDeliveries']._serialized_options = b'\222A\260\007\n\013Log Streams\022\032List log stream deliveries\032\216\005Returns the events sent to this destination, most recent first, each with its current delivery state. Use this to confirm events are arriving and to diagnose a destination that is rejecting them. One entry is returned per event regardless of how many times it was retried; a failed entry carries the time of its next scheduled retry, and ListLogStreamDeliveryAttempts returns that event\'s full attempt history with the destination\'s response. Narrow the results with the event_types, status, after and before filters; status matches an event\'s current state, so an event that failed and then succeeded reads as delivered. Event payloads are not returned.Jd\n\003200\022]\n\036Deliveries for this log stream\022;\n9\0327.scalekit.v1.logstreams.ListLogStreamDeliveriesResponseJ8\n\003403\0221\n/Log streaming is not enabled for this workspaceJT\n\003404\022M\nKLog stream not found - no log stream with this id exists in the environment\202\265\030\002\030D\372\322\344\223\002\t\022\007PREVIEW\202\323\344\223\002$\022\"/api/v1/logstreams/{id}/deliveries'
